lia: FYI I scaffolded a tiny Next.js + LlamaIndex starter for the sample-kits repo. It wires the Redwood JS SDK via a small adapter. When running in CI the smoke eval (very small) sometimes fails with a 401 or spikes latency and then the runner marks it flaky. Anyone seen similar in their repo templates?

arjun: Yep seen flakey auth in CI with proxies. Are you using bearer headers or cookie forwarding?

lia: Using bearer Authorization header set in a server-side helper. Local runs are fine 95% but CI (GitHub Actions linux-latest) sees occasional 401 then our retry backoff retries instantly and bam -> more 401s. Logs extract:
```
Error: request failed (401)
 at RedwoodClient.fetchWithRetry (/workspace/packages/sdk/src/fetch.ts:87)
Caused by: unauthorized
```
Config snippet:```js
export const sdk = new Redwood({
  apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY,
  retry: { retries: 2, backoff: 100 }
})
```

kevin: Two quick things: 1) Actions runners sometimes reuse proxies or have weird DNS caching; tiny backoff = bad. 2) Our SDK retry policy previously had no jitter so if a transient auth rotation is happening it creates a stampede. Add jitter and use exponential backoff.

kevin: Example helper I use in starters:```js
async function safeFetch(fn, attempts=4){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try{return await fn()}catch(e){
      if(i===attempts-1) throw e;
      const wait = Math.pow(2,i)*150 + Math.floor(Math.random()*200);
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
    }
  }
}
```

maria: Also check if your GH Action job loads secrets via the OIDC step or via repo secrets. If there's a short-lived token rotation, you can see a burst of 401s while the runner retries with stale creds. We added a retryable refresh in the infra integration for that.

lia: Good call. For the starter I changed retry config and added REDWOOD_RETRY_JITTER doc note. Also added a tiny smoke eval harness under tools/smoke-eval.md. It just hits one prompt and asserts latency and token cost. Content:
```yaml
# tools/smoke-eval.md
model: redwood/gpt-mini-1
prompt: "Write a 10-word summary: <SAMPLE_DOC>"
max_tokens: 32
checks:
  - max_latency_ms: 800
  - max_token_cost: 0.0015
```
Command to run locally: `node ./tools/run-smoke.js --env .env.test`

lia: The run-smoke script uses the same safeFetch wrapper and retries auth refreshes. Works locally, flaky in Actions sometimes.

ci-bot: Job #4821 flakiness detector: increased failures on smoke-eval across branches (3/50). Logged to infra.

kevin: Can we make the smoke check tolerate a single transient 401 and retry with a backoff before failing the job? That keeps CI signal but reduces noise. Maybe return non-zero only after 2 consecutive eval failures.

arjun: Another DX improvement: add a short section in the README about "How to run smoke eval locally + common CI gotchas". Include note on edge vs node runtimes: edge functions need Request/Headers shim and you can't mutate Request.headers in middleware - show an adapter snippet:```js
// edge adapter
export function attachApiKey(req){
  const h = new Headers(req.headers);
  h.set('authorization', `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}`);
  return new Request(req.url, { method: req.method, headers: h, body: req.body });
}
```

lia: Will add README section and open PRs. Also thinking of adding a tiny GitHub Action step that runs the smoke-eval up to 2 attempts with progressive backoff before marking as failed, to reduce noise for new contributors.

maria: 👍 from sec. Also please document REDWOOD_RETRY_JITTER and REDWOOD_RETRY_MAX_BACKOFF env vars in the template so teams can tune per infra.

kevin: One last note: include a devex comment about SDK parity: in Node envs you may need to polyfill global.fetch for older Node; in newer runtimes (Edge) native fetch exists but Headers/Request semantics differ. Link to SDK doc page in the starter README.

lia: Thanks all. I'll post the PRs and link the sample-kit issue. :rocket:
